:Namespace Board
    ⍝ Representation of the board and the game state.

    ⎕IO ⎕ML←1

    initBoard←{
        ⍝ Initialise the starting position.
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ empty
        ⍝ ← ←→ bitboards, game state; as initFromFEN

        ⍝ Positions are only ever built from FEN, so there is a single
        ⍝ initialisation path.
        initFromFEN 'rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1'
    }

    initFromFEN ←{
        ⍝ Initialise a position from a FEN string. The input is not validated.
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ FEN string or vector of FEN fields
        ⍝ ← ←→ two-element vector consisting of:
        ⍝      bitboards: Boolean matrix, one row per piece.
        ⍝      game state: vector encoding the current game state.

        ⍝ Split the FEN string into its fields.
        f←' '(≠⊆⊢)⍣(1=≡⍵)⊢⍵
        ⍝ Set defaults for halfmove and fullmove.
        f,←((≢f)-4)↓(,'0')(,'1')
        (pieces side castling en_passant halfmove fullmove)←f

        ⍝ A digit stands for that many empty squares. The piece description
        ⍝ is expanded by writing each empty square as ".".
        pieces←pieces~'/'
        digits←pieces∊⎕D
        pieces_expanded←'.'@(∊∘⎕D)pieces/⍨(~digits)+digits×¯1+⎕D⍳pieces

        ⍝ Each FEN letter is paired with its piece by name, so the bitboard
        ⍝ rows follow the encoding given in Pieces.
        ⍝ FEN lists rank 8 first. The bitboards run a1 to h8.
        fen_letters←'PNBRQKpnbrqk'
        piece_ids←##.Pieces.(P N B R Q K p n b r q k)
        squares←(piece_ids,0)[fen_letters⍳,⊖8 8⍴pieces_expanded]
        bitboards←(⍳≢piece_ids)∘.=squares

        game_state←##.GameState.init (
            side:side≡,'b'
            castling_rights:'KQkq'∊castling
            en_passant_square:{⍵≡,'-':0 ⋄ ('abcdefgh'⍳⊃⍵)+8×¯1+'12345678'⍳⊃⌽⍵}en_passant
            halfmove:⊃2⊃⎕VFI halfmove
            fullmove:⊃2⊃⎕VFI fullmove
        )

        bitboards game_state
    }

:EndNamespace
